  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given two integers A,BA, BA,B. You have to choose an integer XXX in the range [minimum(A,BA, BA,B), maximum(A,BA, BA,B)] such that:\n\n⌈B−X2⌉+⌈X−A2⌉\\Big \\lceil \\frac{B - X}{2} \\Big \\rceil + \\Big \\lceil \\frac{X - A}{2} \\Big \\rceil⌈2B−X​⌉+⌈2X−A​⌉ is maximum.\n\nWhat is the maximum sum you can obtain if you choose XXX optimally?\n\n**Note:** ⌈x⌉\\lceil x \\rceil⌈x⌉ : Returns the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to xxx (i.e  rounds up to the nearest integer). For example, ⌈1.4⌉=2\\lceil 1.4 \\rceil = 2⌈1.4⌉=2, ⌈5⌉=5\\lceil 5 \\rceil = 5⌈5⌉=5, ⌈−1.5⌉=−1\\lceil -1.5 \\rceil = -1⌈−1.5⌉=−1, ⌈−3⌉=−3\\lceil -3 \\rceil = -3⌈−3⌉=−3 , ⌈0⌉=0\\lceil 0 \\rceil = 0⌈0⌉=0.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, number of testcases. Then the testcases follow.\nEach testcase contains of a single line of input, two integers A,BA, BA,B.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each testcase, output the maximum sum of ⌈B−X2⌉+⌈X−A2⌉\\lceil \\frac{B - X}{2} \\rceil + \\lceil \\frac{X - A}{2} \\rceil⌈2B−X​⌉+⌈2X−A​⌉.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤A,B≤1091 \\leq A, B \\leq 10^91≤A,B≤109"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2 2\n1 11\n13 6",
        "output": "0\n6\n-3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nIn the first test case, there is only one possible value of XXX which is equal to 222. So the sum is equal to ⌈2−22⌉+⌈2−22⌉\\lceil \\frac{2 - 2}{2} \\rceil + \\lceil \\frac{2 - 2}{2} \\rceil⌈22−2​⌉+⌈22−2​⌉ = ⌈ 0⌉+⌈ 0⌉\\lceil \\ 0 \\rceil + \\lceil \\ 0 \\rceil⌈ 0⌉+⌈ 0⌉  = 0+0=00 + 0 = 00+0=0.\n\n\nIn the second test case, we can choose XXX to be 222. So sum is equal to ⌈11−22⌉+⌈2−12⌉\\lceil \\frac{11 - 2}{2} \\rceil + \\lceil \\frac{2 - 1}{2} \\rceil⌈211−2​⌉+⌈22−1​⌉ = ⌈ 4.5⌉+⌈ 0.5⌉\\lceil \\ 4.5 \\rceil + \\lceil \\ 0.5 \\rceil⌈ 4.5⌉+⌈ 0.5⌉ = 5+1=65 + 1 = 65+1=6. There is no possible way to choose an integer XXX in the range [1,11][1, 11][1,11] such that sum is greater than 666."
      }
    ]
  },
